# ESO path search — frozen default

Nirnside finds the player's files **by itself**. This search is a finished
product default. Do **not** invent a new scheme, reorder folders, walk more
disks, or "fix" EU vs NA paths while working on any other patch. Change it only
when the product owner explicitly asks to change discovery.

Canonical Windows example (EU, Steam/PC, OneDrive Documents):

`C:\Users\<account>\OneDrive\Documents\Elder Scrolls Online\live\SavedVariables\NirnsideSnapshot.lua`

That shape must keep working without Setup, env vars, or `data/incoming`.

## Do not confuse folder name with megaserver

- The live game writes under `Documents\Elder Scrolls Online\<env>\SavedVariables\`.
- `<env>` is `live`, `liveeu`, or `pts` — **not** "EU = liveeu, NA = live".
- Steam/PC **EU is often `live`**, same folder name as NA. Region lives in the
  snapshot (`region` flag), not the folder.
- Search order inside one ESO root is `liveeu`, then `live`, then `pts`, then
  any other folder that already has `SavedVariables`. **First existing file wins.**
  Do not pick "newest", "largest", or "the EU one".

## Where to look (and where not to)

Implementation lives in `src/lib/snapshot/locate.ts` (plus
`windows-known-folders.ts`, `resolve-path.ts`, `install-addons.ts`, `auto.ts`).
Reuse those functions. Do not fork a second search.

Precedence for `NirnsideSnapshot.lua`:

1. `NIRNSIDE_SV_FILE` / `NIRNSIDE_SV_DIR` (escape hatch)
2. Setup-chosen snapshot file (never an incoming path)
3. Auto-detected ESO Documents trees
4. `data/incoming/NirnsideSnapshot.lua` — **machines without ESO only**
5. Bundled `data/sample/Nirnside.lua` — opt-in demo only

Documents trees: Windows known folders (`GetFolderPath('MyDocuments')`),
OneDrive / OneDrive Consumer / Commercial, `Documents` under home and
`USERPROFILE`, any `OneDrive*` folder, localized Documents names. Chosen
`esoDir` and `NIRNSIDE_ESO_DIR` sit in front of those roots.

**Never walk A–Z drive letters** to find SavedVariables or AddOns. A disconnected
network letter blocks `stat` and freezes the Windows exe at 98%. Only use the
profile / system drive implied by `USERPROFILE` / `SystemDrive` / `homedir`.
WSL may look at `/mnt/<letter>/Users` when that mount already exists.

`data/incoming` is a drop-in for this repo/cloud box. It is not the player's
live file. Never treat incoming or the bundled sample as a live account when a
real SavedVariables file exists or was seen before. Sample (`@AzuraStar`) must
not replace a live account.

The file on disk is `SavedVariables\NirnsideSnapshot.lua` (addon name). Do not
look for `Nirnside.lua` in SavedVariables. Do not pick the addon program at
`AddOns\NirnsideSnapshot\NirnsideSnapshot.lua`.

## Addons and Setup

Install **only** `NirnsideSnapshot` and `NirnsideCatalog` into every `AddOns`
folder under the same `esoRoots()` / `envFolders()` discovery. Do not invent
another AddOns walk.

Setup may accept Documents, the `Elder Scrolls Online` folder, `live` / `liveeu`
/ `pts`, `SavedVariables`, or the `.lua` file. Zero-config must still find the
file when the player just starts `Nirnside.exe` on the same PC as the game.

## Feature-work rule

If a task is about currencies, skills, dailies, UI, or anything else: **leave
this search alone**. Do not "improve" it, do not add a new env var as the
default, do not require the user to pick a folder again.
